@startuml decision-flip-redelivery
title Why a Loss-Episode Claim Alone Isn't Enough — Both Redelivery Directions

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

participant "proximity.candidates\n(Kafka)" as PC #FCE7F3
participant "Alert Evaluator" as AE #DBEAFE
participant "alert-state /\nrecent-loss (Redis)" as Redis #FEF9C3
participant "alerts (Kafka)" as AT #D1FAE5

== Direction 1 — a published COMPOSITE must not downgrade on replay ==

PC -> AE : deliver candidate (attempt 1)
AE -> Redis : CLAIM succeeds
AE -> AT : publish COMPOSITE

note over PC, AT
  CRASH before this proximity.candidates
  message's own offset commits.
end note

PC -> AE : redeliver the SAME candidate (attempt 2)
AE -> Redis : loss episode already\ncomposite_issued=1 / claimed

note right of AE
  Without a decision record: naive logic
  re-derives "not eligible" from the NOW-
  claimed episode and gets it backwards.
end note

AE -> AT : (wrong) publish UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY
note over AT
  Two different alert types, two different
  deterministic IDs, for ONE candidate --
  not a harmless idempotent duplicate.
end note

== Direction 2 — an UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY must not upgrade on replay ==

PC -> AE : deliver candidate (attempt 1)
AE -> Redis : no qualifying loss episode found
AE -> AT : publish UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY

note over PC, AT
  CRASH before this proximity.candidates
  message's own offset commits.
end note

... the signal-loss scan runs independently,\nopening a fresh alert-state episode ...

PC -> AE : redeliver the SAME candidate (attempt 2)
AE -> Redis : loss episode now qualifies

note right of AE
  Without a decision record: naive logic
  re-runs CP2 fresh against changed state
  and gets a DIFFERENT answer than attempt 1.
end note

AE -> AT : (wrong) publish COMPOSITE

@enduml
